{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"aee4022f-d3ec-4724-bc1a-55a9211f4ff6","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Implemented the analytics events defined in **docs/EVENTS.md** for the registration flow and the offers list, leveraging the existing `Analytics` wrapper.\n\nKey changes include:\n\n* Added import of `analytics.dart` (via relative path) to both screens.\n* Introduced flags in `RegistrationScreen` to ensure one‑time events (`registration_email_started`, `registration_phone_started`, `terms_accepted`).\n* Updated `TextField.onChanged` callbacks to fire the corresponding events only once.\n* Switched the loan‑amount slider to use `onChangeEnd` for a single `loan_amount_changed` event with the selected amount.\n* Modified the “Continue” button to capture `registration_continue_tapped` with `amount` and `terms` before navigation.\n* Wrapped the offers list in a `NotificationListener\u003cScrollEndNotification\u003e` to emit `offers_scrolled` with the scroll offset.\n* Ensured no PII is sent (email/phone values omitted).\n\nThe colleague’s note guided the implementation:\n- Use a flag to fire text‑field events once per visit.  \n- Move slider analytics to `onChangeEnd`.  \n- Capture scroll analytics via `ScrollEndNotification`.  \n\nAll event names and properties match the specification, while reducing unnecessary event volume.\n\nYou can review the full summary here: **[ANSWER.md](file:///Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/aee4022f-d3ec-4724-bc1a-55a9211f4ff6/ANSWER.md)**.\n","duration_seconds":101.34901,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":20664,"output_tokens":7958,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":244544,"total_tokens":28622}}}
